Since $p∦q,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =-2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329676 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29c5c7fe-9e8b-501e-8d99-9eaa01e9d9ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327291} {:answer/id #uuid "561d0092-52f2-5240-85dd-94406071feea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327678} {:answer/id #uuid "6f77438e-da55-563e-a052-19d551e6520a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327900} {:answer/id #uuid "be6c2167-cf77-5c18-b9a9-c5f9e8dffcf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328597} {:answer/id #uuid "c1ea5c82-4696-5794-899e-2fbfedfbd836" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-4$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1ea5c82-4696-5794-899e-2fbfedfbd836" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-4$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328628} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0f8ee01-9c68-5cfd-a230-414249ca8bcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329456}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c824c20-e7d8-5ee0-a1d9-a9f4762eb921" :question/math-academy-id "q-42662" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2f149fb4f32fb264e0af6898e7737d570ec90bbff31cf1256eb9bd2636ceab3.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $w=\\lambda u+\\mu v$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/58/589f9f524a7c98da61ad6c5001b8d392d89073d5734cd70cfa750d153fe6f7b7.png)\n\nIn $△OUW$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OU=2|v|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OU}$ has the opposite direction to $v$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=-2v.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $UW=4|u|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{UW}$ has the opposite direction to $u$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{UW}=-4u.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =-2v-4u \\\\  & =-4u-2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $w=\\lambda u+\\mu v=-4u-2v.$\n\nSince $u∦v,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-4$ and $\\mu =-2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cfbd0cb-8733-5454-bc51-0705f00c775a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327184} {:answer/id #uuid "453cbc37-f1de-5673-a82f-603e75313e66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327538} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb803a8-19e2-5f29-aee8-b53dd044f6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327629} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca86f5b-66fb-523f-889e-3c74b76af03b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327871} {:answer/id #uuid "c00cff55-58e1-5cdc-9c57-9569e58b8ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fb803a8-19e2-5f29-aee8-b53dd044f6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327629} :answer-field/id #uuid "11b673e4-f9d9-54b5-824e-58d311d04d42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329216}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff56059b-