dent :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301211} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa3c4a6c-7827-538e-a831-35325998bb72" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301774}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "192ab3c2-7926-59cc-a0a7-34dbb7dda250" :question/math-academy-id "q-322575" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d9448f9f05666f9806975b37a73f09c492eb73139b6f9395b619f077f3a584c9.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OP}=p,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q,$ and $R$ divides $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ in the ratio $PR:RQ=4:9.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OR}$ via the vectors $p$ and $q.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OR}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$p+$\n{{field-2}}\n$q$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OR}=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OP}=p,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{PR}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OPQ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{PO}+\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\  & =-p+q \\\\  & =q-p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $PR:RQ=4:9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PR}=\\frac{4}{13}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=\\frac{4}{13}(q-p).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OR} & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\  & =p+\\frac{4}{13}(q-p) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{13}p+\\frac{4}{13}q.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302114 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b14b714-b52b-5d04-b557-997d58e4906b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b14b714-b52b-5d04-b557-997d58e4906b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300742} :answer-fiel